# {{.ServiceName}}

Go microservice generated with `servicegen`.

## Structure

```text
api/                  OpenAPI contract and HTTP handlers
cmd/                  application entry point
gen/                  generated OpenAPI code
internal/service/     orchestration, transactions, external calls
internal/domain/      aggregates, state transitions, rules, policies
internal/repository/  persistence and database entities
migrations/           database migrations
observability/         Prometheus, Grafana, and Alloy integration files
```

## Run

```bash
make tools
make generate
make run
```

The service listens on `http://localhost:{{.HTTPPort}}`.

Copy `.env.example` to `.env` when you want to change local settings. Real environment variables have priority over values from `.env`.

Swagger UI is available at `http://localhost:{{.HTTPPort}}/docs` and Prometheus metrics at `http://localhost:{{.HTTPPort}}/metrics`.

Healthcheck:

```text
GET http://localhost:{{.HTTPPort}}/health
```

Every HTTP response contains `X-Request-ID`. The same value is written to the structured JSON log and attached to the OpenTelemetry span. Traces are sent to `localhost:4319` by default; database initialization is disabled until `DB_ENABLED=true`.

See `observability/README.md` for connection steps for Prometheus, Grafana, Loki, Alloy, and Jaeger.
